==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|ydropsy|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|idropsie|lang=fro}}, {{term|ydropisie|lang=fro}}, from  {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|hydropisis|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|ὕδρωψ||lang=grc}}, from {{term|ὕδωρ||water|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|dropsies}}

# {{context|pathology|lang=en}} Swelling, [[edema]], often from chronic obstructive pulmonary disease [[COPD]].
#* '''1911''', ''Joseph Addison'', [[S:1911 Encyclopædia Britannica/Addison, Joseph|Encyclopædia Britannica]]:
#*: The disease under which Addison laboured appears to have been asthma. It became more violent after his retirement from office, and was now accompanied by '''dropsy'''.

